drm/msm/dpu: let command-mode panels pace frames by TE only (sync_cfg_height).

The tear check reloads its line counter with vdisplay on every TE and
generates an internal vsync when the counter reaches sync_cfg_height.
Mainline uses 2 * vtotal, which on the Xiaomi 12 panel leaves only ~41 us of
margin at 120 Hz (8.610 ms vs the measured 8.569 ms TE period) and makes the
DPU self-trigger on every frame at 60 Hz, starting transfers that collide
with the panel's scan-out of its compressed GRAM. Stock (downstream SDE)
programs 0xfff0, so the panel's TE alone paces frames.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
@@ -382,7 +382,13 @@
 	 * TE event coming from the display TE pin we won't stall immediately
 	 */
 	tc_cfg.hw_vsync_mode = 1;
-	tc_cfg.sync_cfg_height = mode->vtotal * 2;
+	/*
+	 * Downstream uses 0xfff0: never self-trigger, let the TE pace frames.
+	 * vtotal * 2 left almost no margin on the Xiaomi 12 panel (TE period
+	 * longer than the nominal mode) and caused transfers to collide with
+	 * scan-out.
+	 */
+	tc_cfg.sync_cfg_height = 0xfff0;
 	tc_cfg.vsync_init_val = mode->vdisplay;
 	tc_cfg.sync_threshold_start = DEFAULT_TEARCHECK_SYNC_THRESH_START;
 	tc_cfg.sync_threshold_continue = DEFAULT_TEARCHECK_SYNC_THRESH_CONTINUE;
